arrival, hub dwell (arrival to first attempt), and first attempt to final status."}, {"id": "P6", "text": "Normalise Weight (`0.5`, `0.50 kg`, `500 g`, `0.5kg`, `500gm`) to kilograms and deal with the zero weights, normalise Attempts (`2`, `2 attempts`, `Two`), and clean Pincode (`226010`, `226010.0`, `226 010`). Then check that Zone is consistent with the destination city."}]}, {"key": "sql", "title": "Phase 2, SQL: Answer the Business Questions", "tasks": [{"id": "S10", "text": "Compare peak season (15 Oct to 20 Nov) with the rest of the year per destination hub: volume, average dwell and true on-time %. Which hubs absorbed the peak badly?"}, {"id": "S9", "text": "Build a weight slab (0-0.5, 0.5-1, 1-2, 2-5, 5+ kg) x zone x service profit table and return the loss-making cells with at least 100 shipments."}, {"id": "S6", "text": "For each zone x service type: the promised days (promised minus pickup), the median actual days to final delivery, and the true on-time %. Where is the promise itself unrealistic?"}, {"id": "S7", "text": "Compare COD vs Prepaid: first-attempt failure rate (a shipment with an NDR Reason logged), RTO rate, average attempts per shipment and profit per shipment."}, {"id": "S2", "text": "Compute the on-time figure a shipper would compute: Delivered shipments with a final status date on or before the promised date, as a share of all shipments that reached a final status (exclude In Transit). Show it next to S1 per month and report the gap."}, {"id": "S11", "text": "Quantify the cost of failure: total rupees spent on second and third attempts and on RTO legs, split by NDR reason and by hub."}, {"id": "S12", "text": "Using a CTE, build a per-shipper funnel: picked up -> reached a first attempt -> delivered on the first attempt -> delivered eventually -> delivered on time."}, {"id": "S1", "text": "Reproduce the Ops dashboard's on-time figure: the share of shipments whose FIRST ATTEMPT date is on or before the promised date (among shipments that had an attempt), per month and overall."}, {"id": "S4", "text": "For each rider, the share of their logged NDR reasons that are Customer Not Available, alongside their escalation rate and their share of the network's volume. Flag riders more than 2x the network average on the first measure."}, {"id": "S8", "text": "Profit per shipment by shipper, ranked, with shipment count and share of COD. Which shippers cost the network money?"}, {"id": "S3", "text": "Using window functions, rank all 48 riders by volume, by first-attempt on-time % and by true on-time %. Return the riders in the top 5 on first-attempt on-time but in the bottom 15 on true on-time."}, {"id": "S5", "text": "Average days between Hub Arrival and First Attempt, per destination hub and per weekday of arrival. Which hub and which days are outliers?"}]}, {"key": "dash1", "title": "Phase 3a, Dashboard Page 1: Shipment Lookup", "tasks": [{"id": "D5", "text": "Make the shipment-results table itself filterable and sortable by any visible column, so someone can browse instead of only searching by exact AWB."}, {"id": "D3", "text": "Add a date-range filter on Pickup Date and a separate date-range filter on Final Status Date, and make sure both can be applied together."}, {"id": "D1", "text": "Build a search box that takes an AWB number and shows the whole journey on one screen: pickup, hub arrival, each attempt, final status, with the promised date marked and the delay (or slack) called out, plus the billing waterfall (billed minus each cost = profit)."}, {"id": "D2", "text": "On the same screen show context: shipper, service and zone, rider and vehicle, NDR reasons, proof of delivery, escalation flag, CSAT and remarks."}, {"id": "D4", "text": "Add filters for Shipper, Destination Hub, Zone, Service Type, Delivery Status and Rider that combine with the date filters (AND logic) rather than replacing them."}]}, {"key": "dash2", "title": "Phase 3b, Dashboard Page 2: Analytics", "tasks": [{"id": "D13", "text": "Add a peak-season panel comparing peak and non-peak per hub on volume, dwell and true on-time %."}, {"id": "D8", "text": "Add a hub x weekday-of-arrival heatmap of average dwell or on-time %, with the outlier cells unmistakable."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Pickup Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Add a weight-slab x zone profit matrix with loss-making cells highlighted and shipment counts shown."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a rider scorecard showing volume, first-attempt on-time %, true on-time %, RTO % and escalation rate side by side, so 'best rider' is never reduced to one number."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add an NDR panel: failed-attempt reasons by payment type and by rider, with the rupee cost of failure."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel with the dashboard's on-time % and the true on-time % on the same chart, so the gap between them is the story."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Add a promise-vs-reality panel: for each zone x service, the promised days against the actual distribution of delivery days."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Add a shipper panel: volume, true on-time %, COD share and profit per shipment."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a geography panel: true on-time % and profit by state, with the best and worst five towns called out."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format: Word, PDF, Notion, a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you went from the raw export to cleaned data to SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made, especially how you resolved rider identity and treated the cut-off; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3-5 findings, stated the way a network head wants to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed recommendations for what Raahi Express should do before next peak season. This is the deliverable a hiring manager would actually read, so treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how many shipments and how many points of on-time % the network would recover if the worst hub's weekday problem disappeared. Show the arithmetic."}, {"id": "X-S6", "text": "Analyse Lost and Damaged shipments: claim cost by hub, shipper and declared value, and whether any pattern suggests a fixable cause."}, {"id": "X-S3", "text": "Design a COD policy (a surcharge, a minimum value, or prepaid-only in some zones) and estimate its effect on profit and RTO using the data."}]}]}$pack$::jsonb
from public.datasets where slug = 'late-again-last-mile-fy2526'
on conflict (license_code) do nothing;

