ommendations for what Raahi Express should do before next peak season. This is the deliverable a hiring manager would actually read, so treat it that way."}]}, {"key": "stretch", "title": "Stretch ideas (optional)", "tasks": [{"id": "X-S3", "text": "Design a COD policy (a surcharge, a minimum value, or prepaid-only in some zones) and estimate its effect on profit and RTO using the data."}, {"id": "X-S2", "text": "Estimate how many shipments and how many points of on-time % the network would recover if the worst hub's weekday problem disappeared. Show the arithmetic."}, {"id": "X-S1", "text": "Propose a new promised-days table per zone x service that would hit about 90% true on-time, and say what it does to the competitiveness of Zone D offers."}]}], "premium": [{"id": "X3", "text": "**Build and defend a rider scorecard.** Combine volume, first-attempt success, true on-time %, RTO rate and escalations into one weighted score. Run a sensitivity analysis showing how the top 10 changes as you vary each weight by +/-10%, and say which weighting you would recommend."}, {"id": "X4", "text": "**Forecast next quarter.** Using the 12 months of history, forecast Q1 FY26-27 (Apr-Jun 2026) shipments per hub and flag which hubs will hit capacity problems, treating the peak season sensibly."}, {"id": "X1", "text": "**Normalize it.** Design a 3NF relational schema (separate tables for riders, hubs, shippers and shipments at minimum) from the flat file, load it into a real SQL database, and rewrite your S3 and S10 answers as proper JOIN queries."}, {"id": "X5", "text": "**Set the promise scientifically.** For each zone x service, use the empirical distribution of delivery days to choose the promised days that hit a target on-time rate, and quantify the trade-off between a tighter promise and a higher breach rate."}, {"id": "X2", "text": "**Prove the weekday gap is real.** One hub shows a dramatic on-time drop for shipments arriving on certain weekdays. Run a statistical test (two-proportion z-test or logistic regression) and show it survives controlling for service type, zone and peak season."}]}$pack$::jsonb
