b x weekday-of-arrival heatmap of average dwell or on-time %, with the outlier cells unmistakable."}, {"id": "D9", "text": "Add a promise-vs-reality panel: for each zone x service, the promised days against the actual distribution of delivery days."}, {"id": "D7", "text": "Add a monthly trend panel with the dashboard's on-time % and the true on-time % on the same chart, so the gap between them is the story."}, {"id": "D10", "text": "Add an NDR panel: failed-attempt reasons by payment type and by rider, with the rupee cost of failure."}, {"id": "D11", "text": "Add a shipper panel: volume, true on-time %, COD share and profit per shipment."}, {"id": "D15", "text": "Make every panel on Page 2 respect a global date-range filter (Pickup Date), so the whole analytics page can be viewed for any period, not just the full year."}, {"id": "D12", "text": "Add a weight-slab x zone profit matrix with loss-making cells highlighted and shipment counts shown."}, {"id": "D6", "text": "Build a rider scorecard showing volume, first-attempt on-time %, true on-time %, RTO % and escalation rate side by side, so 'best rider' is never reduced to one number."}, {"id": "D13", "text": "Add a peak-season panel comparing peak and non-peak per hub on volume, dwell and true on-time %."}, {"id": "D14", "text": "Add a geography panel: true on-time % and profit by state, with the best and worst five towns called out."}]}, {"key": "documentation", "title": "Phase 4, Documentation", "tasks": [{"id": "DOC1", "text": "Write a short project write-up (any format: Word, PDF, Notion, a README) with three sections: (1) **Process Flow**: how you went from the raw export to cleaned data to SQL answers to your dashboard, including the decisions you made, especially how you resolved rider identity and treated the cut-off; (2) **Key Discoveries**: your top 3-5 findings, stated the way a network head wants to hear them, not as code output; (3) **Future Growth Recommendations**: at least 3 concrete, data-backed rec